10. A website looks great on a laptop but is unreadable on a mobile phone because the user hasto zoom in and scroll horizontally. Identify the design principle 
missing here and explainhow Media Queries/Fluid Grids could fix it.
The design principle missing in this scenario is Responsive Web Design.The website works well on a laptop but becomes unreadable on a mobile phone. This shows 
that the site was not designed to adapt to different screen sizes.Having to zoom in and scroll horizontally makes reading difficult and frustrating for mobile users. This results in a poor user experience and may cause users 
to leave the website.
Media queries allow the website to detect the screen size of the device. Based on this, different CSS styles can be applied so that text, images, and layouts
adjust properly on mobile screens.
Fluid grids use relative units like percentages instead of fixed pixels. This allows the layout to resize smoothly according to the screen width, preventing 
horizontal scrolling.
Using media queries and fluid grids ensures the website is readable and usable on all devices, improves user experience, and makes the website truly responsive.
